{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f68bb507d59a5ced64d353d598c76e8b7959771b4ee5579148b14f33825aff4","digest":{"component_or_area":"documentation and CI gates","key_entities":[".github/complexity-baseline.json",".github/module-size-limit.txt","scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","pyproject.toml [tool.ruff.lint.mccabe]","AGENTS.md","make lint","ruff check --select C901"],"problem_keywords":["C901","cyclomatic complexity","ratchet","structural gate","documentation","CI gate","AGENTS.md","module size policy"],"propositions":["AGENTS.md documents the module-size gate (800 LOC) but omits the C901 shrink-only complexity ratchet, leaving implementers unaware of the structural constraint until CI fails","The C901 ratchet enforces per-symbol McCabe complexity ceiling (15 max, stored in .github/complexity-baseline.json) and fails when functions gain new or increased complexity, even when total LOC and other lints pass","Routine changes like adding CLI flags or guard clauses predictably trigger the ratchet, forcing unplanned behavior-preserving refactoring at pre-flight rather than during design","The remedy is extraction-not-baseline-bump (shrink-only, never bump the ceiling), discoverable via ruff check --select C901 or scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787669910938072001,"uuid":"117c0a34-a467-406c-bf5c-dceb62f1f794"}